    <briefdescription>
<para>Hybrid Logical <ref refid="test__storage__latency__bench_8cpp_1a19bfb27380067c74ae297dd7dad5fb37" kindref="member">Clock</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Thread-safe monotonic clock that combines wall-clock time with a logical counter to provide a total order of events, even across nodes that exchange HLC-stamped messages.</para>
<para>API: <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_hybrid_logical_clock_1ae38c1af4ba580e51fb8509facd062126" kindref="member">now()</ref> - generate a new timestamp for a local event update(received) - advance the clock on receiving a remote timestamp <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_hybrid_logical_clock_1ac91221194b156ee575a27f6ff25db549" kindref="member">peek()</ref> - read the current timestamp without advancing it </para>
    </detaileddescription>
